senses.gloss:
iñjita (= Pali id.),
(1) primarily ppp. of iñjate, q.v.; see iñjita-tva;
(2) subst. nt., motion, movement (literal and physical): Mv 〔i.305.21〕 (vs) prāsādikeʼ iṃjitena (read ijitena; 〔§ 2.73〕; cf. ijya- forms s.v. iñjate) praviśantāṃ (buddhasya śrāvakān), entering with serene walk;
(3) subst. nt., mobility, vacillation, unsteadiness; = iñjana or ˚nā, and like these often associated with manyanā (or manyita), spandita (miswritten sya˚), and other qualities deprecated in religious life: Mvy 〔7218〕 ˚tam = Tib. gyo ba, foll. by syanditam; SP 〔336.3〕 (vs) varjitvā iñjitā (v.l. ˚tān) manyitāni ca; 〔372.7〕 (prose) iñjita-manyitaprapañcitāni jñāsyati; Dbh 〔64.13〕 sarveñjita-manyanāsyandita-vikalpāpagato bhavati; Bbh 〔339.18〕 (prose) (-abhiniveśa-, q.v.) -sarveñjitāni … prahīyante; 〔340.21〕 sarvābhiniveśeñjitaprahāṇataś ca. See also an-iñjita.
